  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of yellow-green fog centered on a point within range. The fog lasts for the duration or until strong wind (such as the one created by <em>Gust of Wind</em>) disperses it, ending the spell. Its area is Heavily Obscured.</p><p>Each creature in the Sphere makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 5d8 Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature must also make this save when the Sphere moves into its space and when it enters the Sphere or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn.</p><p>The Sphere moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5.</p><p><strong>midi-qol</strong>: Built from region behaviours, no macro. The Cast activity is a Utility activity that places a 20-foot-radius sphere Region; it rolls nothing itself. Its <em>Region Behavior</em> settings (All dispositions, caster not excluded, once per turn) attach midi's region activity behaviour with two rules, <em>Entry</em> and <em>Turn End</em>, both running the automation-only <em>Cloudkill Damage</em> save activity (identifier <code>cloudkillDamage</code>) for the creature concerned. Foundry treats creatures already in the area as entering when the behaviour is created, so they make the initial save, and once per turn stops a second save at the end of that turn. Its <em>Move Each Turn</em> setting (10 ft, away from the caster, start of the caster's turn) moves the cloud in combat; creatures it passes over enter it and save. Out of combat, drag the Region. Spell scaling is kept (+1d8 per slot above 5th). Ending concentration deletes the Region. Heavily Obscured is not automated.</p>",
      "chat": "<p>You create a 20-foot-radius Sphere of yellow-green fog centered on a point within range. The fog lasts for the duration or until strong wind (such as the one created by <em>Gust of Wind</em>) disperses it, ending the spell. Its area is Heavily Obscured.</p><p>Each creature in the Sphere makes a Constitution saving throw, taking 5d8 Poison damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature must also make this save when the Sphere moves into its space and when it enters the Sphere or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn.</p><p>The Sphere moves 10 feet away from you at the start of each of your turns.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The damage increases by 1d8 for each spell slot level above 5.</p>"
    },
